   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the tax law, in relation to authorizing the county of Cortland\nto impose a tax on real estate transfers; and providing for the repeal of such\nprovisions upon expiration thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S3603",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S3603-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add Art 31-I §§1449-aaaaaaa - 1449-ppppppp, Tax L",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S3603\n\nSPONSOR: WEBB\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the tax law, in relation to authorizing the county of\nCortland to impose a tax on real estate transfers; and providing for the\nrepeal of such provisions upon expiration thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE:;\n\nAmending Article 31 of the New York State Tax law to permit Cortland\nCounty to Impose a Tax on the Transfer of Real Property\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nCortland County Legislature requested an Amendment to New York State Tax\nLaw authorizing the County to impose and collect a local transfer tax of\none dollars ($1.00) when the consideration exceeds five hundred dollars\n($500.00), at the rate of one dollar for each five hundred dollars, or\nfractional part thereof,\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nCounty of Cortland passed a resolution No 45-21\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2022: S.6167-A Died in Senate Budget and Revenue Committee\n\n2021: S.6167-A Died in Senate Budget and Revenue Committee\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nUndetermined\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
